(2736991, 380993, 27373, '<td valign="top">Bad Hair Day.</td>', 'Bad Hair Day.', '2006-08-17 15:08:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2737353, 381194, 27373, '<td valign="top">We need to speak about this unnatural growth out of your babies chest.  Cute.</td>', 'We need to speak about this unnatural growth out of your babies chest.  Cute.', '2006-08-17 17:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2737381, 380849, 61679, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: This image has very little detail of the camera visible and it could use more contrast.  You could have used a couple of reflectors (white poster board or crumpled aluminum foil) to help direct some light between you and the water to improve the detail issue.  The contrast issue is fixable using a number of post processing tools, like brightness/contrast, levels, or curves.  I''m not that experienced with curves but I would be willing to play around with your image with levels if you would like to see how it might look.  Feel free to PM me.</td>', 'Back to comment: This image has very little detail of the camera visible and it could use more contrast.  You could have used a couple of reflectors (white poster board or crumpled aluminum foil) to help direct some light between you and the water to improve the detail issue.  The contrast issue is fixable using a number of post processing tools, like brightness/contrast, levels, or curves.  I''m not that experienced with curves but I would be willing to play around with your image with levels if you would like to see how it might look.  Feel free to PM me.', '2006-08-17 17:55:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2737394, 380529, 61679, '<td valign="top">I''m willing to bet by now that more than one person has mentioned that this is supposed to be a picture of your camera taking a picture of itself.  As for the image you did submit, you might want to try adjusting the contrast and brightness to help the Nikon on the strap look brighter and more prominant.  This could also be accomplished using curves or levels.  I think the image could use a little more sharpening after resizing as well.</td>', 'I''m willing to bet by now that more than one person has mentioned that this is supposed to be a picture of your camera taking a picture of itself.  As for the image you did submit, you might want to try adjusting the contrast and brightness to help the Nikon on the strap look brighter and more prominant.  This could also be accomplished using curves or levels.  I think the image could use a little more sharpening after resizing as well.', '2006-08-17 18:00:22.000000', NULL, 1),
