(2739165, 380980, 16004, '<td valign="top">i gave this a 9.  the camera looks fantastic against the yellow orangey fore/back ground, especially with the over-sized nature of the lens on the front.  didn''t quite get the ten because i would have liked the frame of the glasses to be in sharp focus too (the design of them would be better suited to crisp defined lines, i feel) and the skin looks a bit reddy (white balance or a tan?). great shot though.</td>', 'i gave this a 9.  the camera looks fantastic against the yellow orangey fore/back ground, especially with the over-sized nature of the lens on the front.  didn''t quite get the ten because i would have liked the frame of the glasses to be in sharp focus too (the design of them would be better suited to crisp defined lines, i feel) and the skin looks a bit reddy (white balance or a tan?). great shot though.', '2006-08-18 09:46:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739167, 381035, 16004, '<td valign="top">gave this a 7.  i love the beautifully rich red colour of the backdrop; looks really striking against the black of the canera body and lens.  clearly the shot is suffering a bit from the distortion (less solid reflections) from the glass in the mirror, but the overall shot is so strikingly in your face it doesn''t hurt it that much.  nice.</td>', 'gave this a 7.  i love the beautifully rich red colour of the backdrop; looks really striking against the black of the canera body and lens.  clearly the shot is suffering a bit from the distortion (less solid reflections) from the glass in the mirror, but the overall shot is so strikingly in your face it doesn''t hurt it that much.  nice.', '2006-08-18 09:49:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739176, 380529, 16004, '<td valign="top">voted this a 4.  i don''t know really - i salute this because you''ve gone a different way to everyone else and taken a shot of elements of your camera, but then, it''s also like being asked to do a portrait of a person and only photographing their hat and scarf.  doesn''t <i>really</i> meet the challenge, sadly.  i like the actual shot though; the depth of field works and the strap has a certain well used and worn quality.  lighting at the back seems a bit harsh though - somethimes better to illuminate what you''re shooting than light from behind.</td>', 'voted this a 4.  i don''t know really - i salute this because you''ve gone a different way to everyone else and taken a shot of elements of your camera, but then, it''s also like being asked to do a portrait of a person and only photographing their hat and scarf.  doesn''t really meet the challenge, sadly.  i like the actual shot though; the depth of field works and the strap has a certain well used and worn quality.  lighting at the back seems a bit harsh though - somethimes better to illuminate what you''re shooting than light from behind.', '2006-08-18 09:57:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739179, 379394, 16004, '<td valign="top">gave this a big fat 10.  too much i like about it; the lighting is fantastic, the colours being bold and that sort of hueness, the sky nicely dramatic (but not overly so in an unnatural way), the marks and scratches on the surface of the glass, the way the camera is held...  it''s really good striking stuff.  also a great little camera; we have that one and i''m always impressed with it - especially in terms of colour performance...  anyway, excellent.  10.</td>', 'gave this a big fat 10.  too much i like about it; the lighting is fantastic, the colours being bold and that sort of hueness, the sky nicely dramatic (but not overly so in an unnatural way), the marks and scratches on the surface of the glass, the way the camera is held...  it''s really good striking stuff.  also a great little camera; we have that one and i''m always impressed with it - especially in terms of colour performance...  anyway, excellent.  10.', '2006-08-18 10:01:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739192, 381187, 16004, '<td valign="top">gave this an 8.  it''s let down a bit by the splodge of black from the hat right across the top, and the light fitting on the wall (would be better with a plain tiles background methinks).  he could also do with some hands.  but, it''s so madly bonkers that it is impossible not to like it.  having him on the side feels right too...  i also like that it''s one of the few shots that actually incorporates the mirror as an integral part of the overall theme (that is, we''re looking through his eyes), so i guess the hat splodge is in fact suitable...  anyway, well deserved 8, i feel.</td>', 'gave this an 8.  it''s let down a bit by the splodge of black from the hat right across the top, and the light fitting on the wall (would be better with a plain tiles background methinks).  he could also do with some hands.  but, it''s so madly bonkers that it is impossible not to like it.  having him on the side feels right too...  i also like that it''s one of the few shots that actually incorporates the mirror as an integral part of the overall theme (that is, we''re looking through his eyes), so i guess the hat splodge is in fact suitable...  anyway, well deserved 8, i feel.', '2006-08-18 10:10:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739243, 381253, 16004, '<td valign="top">gave this a six.  it''s a good application of the chromey surface, must admit, and i especially like the slightly smeary effect on the camera - visually very lovely.  the ends of the toaster on the other hand doesn''t look that good in terms of complementing the whole shot.   and the bit of bread (in terms of being soft, brown and not really techie like the rest of the image conveys) looks a bit silly and superfluous.  still a likeable shot though.</td>', 'gave this a six.  it''s a good application of the chromey surface, must admit, and i especially like the slightly smeary effect on the camera - visually very lovely.  the ends of the toaster on the other hand doesn''t look that good in terms of complementing the whole shot.   and the bit of bread (in terms of being soft, brown and not really techie like the rest of the image conveys) looks a bit silly and superfluous.  still a likeable shot though.', '2006-08-18 10:43:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739305, 378874, 64035, '<td valign="top">The idea''s interesting, but the net effect is vast amounts of blurred picture.</td>', 'The idea''s interesting, but the net effect is vast amounts of blurred picture.', '2006-08-18 11:11:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739413, 381220, 62018, '<td valign="top">nice try with have camera but with a black camera it just doesn''t work.</td>', 'nice try with have camera but with a black camera it just doesn''t work.', '2006-08-18 12:24:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2739438, 377996, 51750, '<td valign="top">I like this alot, however this is a camera self portrait challenge and thus i think the camera should be the part in focus rather than the person which i geuss is you.</td>', 'I like this alot, however this is a camera self portrait challenge and thus i think the camera should be the part in focus rather than the person which i geuss is you.', '2006-08-18 12:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
