(2748414, 381203, 38732, '<td valign="top">The only waterdrop reflection that I noticed, so you definitely get points for originality.  It might have scored a bit higher from me if the drops were a little bigger, or if there were more drops in the shot, but still a good showing in this challenge.</td>', 'The only waterdrop reflection that I noticed, so you definitely get points for originality.  It might have scored a bit higher from me if the drops were a little bigger, or if there were more drops in the shot, but still a good showing in this challenge.', '2006-08-22 10:34:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2748432, 381194, 38732, '<td valign="top">I''m sure most photographers consider their camera''s their "baby" :)<br/> <br/>Would prefer if the lighting was a little more even for this shot.  Also, I''m not fond of the wrinkled white background.  Perhaps some processing to potentially remove it would draw my attention solely to the subject, instead of being a distraction.  Still, a great idea and a good showing in this challenge.</td>', 'I''m sure most photographers consider their camera''s their "baby" :) Would prefer if the lighting was a little more even for this shot.  Also, I''m not fond of the wrinkled white background.  Perhaps some processing to potentially remove it would draw my attention solely to the subject, instead of being a distraction.  Still, a great idea and a good showing in this challenge.', '2006-08-22 10:39:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2748452, 381268, 38732, '<td valign="top">Another attempt at a DPC favorite, which I don''t mind.  Unfortuntely, I find the camera blends into the black background too much, making the focus of this shot on the white sheet instead.  Perhaps a touch of backlighting to separate the camera from the background, even just a little, might have helped bring it out of the shadows.  Still, a great shot.</td>', 'Another attempt at a DPC favorite, which I don''t mind.  Unfortuntely, I find the camera blends into the black background too much, making the focus of this shot on the white sheet instead.  Perhaps a touch of backlighting to separate the camera from the background, even just a little, might have helped bring it out of the shadows.  Still, a great shot.', '2006-08-22 10:45:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2748464, 381183, 38732, '<td valign="top">Definitely one of the best "dress up" shots in this challenge.  I really like the bright colours against the white background.</td>', 'Definitely one of the best "dress up" shots in this challenge.  I really like the bright colours against the white background.', '2006-08-22 10:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2748468, 379000, 38732, '<td valign="top">I like the effect of the 3-way mirror here, especially with the inclusion of the extra lens and filters.  I''m also a sucker for b/w.  What I''m not too fond of is the wrinkled/dirty(?) sheet and the fact that it doesn''t completely cover the entire background.  Good showing!</td>', 'I like the effect of the 3-way mirror here, especially with the inclusion of the extra lens and filters.  I''m also a sucker for b/w.  What I''m not too fond of is the wrinkled/dirty(?) sheet and the fact that it doesn''t completely cover the entire background.  Good showing!', '2006-08-22 10:52:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2748472, 380699, 38732, '<td valign="top">Ah, figured someone would enter a shot like this, just for the fun factor (Judi?) :)<br/> <br/>I love the sunset, and the purple haze in the sky; gorgeous.  Great photo!</td>', 'Ah, figured someone would enter a shot like this, just for the fun factor (Judi?) :) I love the sunset, and the purple haze in the sky; gorgeous.  Great photo!', '2006-08-22 10:57:37.000000', NULL, 1),
