(2768231, 380566, 49326, '<td valign="top">Vá, snilld. Ég elska litina og yfirlýsinguna í henni. Ég mundi giska á að stærð myndavélarinnar valdi þessari einkunn. Ég hef tekið eftir því að litlum myndefnum gengur ekkert svo rosalega vel í keppnum. En það er allt í lagi, því þetta er snilldar mynd. Ég hlakka til að sjá fleiri myndir eftir þig.</td>', 'Vá, snilld. Ég elska litina og yfirlýsinguna í henni. Ég mundi giska á að stærð myndavélarinnar valdi þessari einkunn. Ég hef tekið eftir því að litlum myndefnum gengur ekkert svo rosalega vel í keppnum. En það er allt í lagi, því þetta er snilldar mynd. Ég hlakka til að sjá fleiri myndir eftir þig.', '2006-08-28 15:51:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2769517, 380993, 45706, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>Nice image you have here and welcome to the DPC challenges!<br/> <br/>The composition is good, but maybe you could get a different crop to where  the camera isn''t too much in the center. I like to color and I think the colors would have popped more with a sharper focus. I also think it would have helped with the defining of the "hair" to stand out more from strand to strand. Also, the reflection on the camera is a little distracting. Furthermore, I think a noise reduction would help this image.<br/> <br/>Overall, I think you have a pretty good idea here and with a little work I think this could be a really neat image.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>:)</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club!  Nice image you have here and welcome to the DPC challenges! The composition is good, but maybe you could get a different crop to where  the camera isn''t too much in the center. I like to color and I think the colors would have popped more with a sharper focus. I also think it would have helped with the defining of the "hair" to stand out more from strand to strand. Also, the reflection on the camera is a little distracting. Furthermore, I think a noise reduction would help this image. Overall, I think you have a pretty good idea here and with a little work I think this could be a really neat image. Keep up the good work! :)', '2006-08-29 01:07:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2770132, 378808, 63244, '<td valign="top">The camera and photo software are VERY new to me.  Still trying to learn what all goes on!  Things will get better I hope.</td>', 'The camera and photo software are VERY new to me.  Still trying to learn what all goes on!  Things will get better I hope.', '2006-08-29 10:52:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2770133, 378076, 62009, '<td valign="top"><b>Greets from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I like the intent of this shot.  It''s different, but has appeal.  I agree that it is quite grainy.  Perhaps if you shot this at a lower ISO.  <br/> <br/>Also, this is a very dark photo.  I think if it were lightened up a bit so we could see more of the camera, it would have done better.<br/> <br/>Overall, I''d have to say that this is a very creative shot, but could have been processed/shot a bit better.<br/> <br/>--Mike</td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club  I like the intent of this shot.  It''s different, but has appeal.  I agree that it is quite grainy.  Perhaps if you shot this at a lower ISO.   Also, this is a very dark photo.  I think if it were lightened up a bit so we could see more of the camera, it would have done better. Overall, I''d have to say that this is a very creative shot, but could have been processed/shot a bit better. --Mike', '2006-08-29 10:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2770298, 380229, 62009, '<td valign="top"><b>Greets from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>This is a very interesting photograph.  I like the B&amp;W conversion, it works very well.  Also, this is completely out of the box and works well.  From the perspective, it seems almost like Chaplin is holding the camera.<br/> <br/>My only complaint is that the bulb is very, very white and draws most of the attention.<br/> <br/>Once again, love the shot.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting.<br/> <br/>--Mike</td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club  This is a very interesting photograph.  I like the B&W conversion, it works very well.  Also, this is completely out of the box and works well.  From the perspective, it seems almost like Chaplin is holding the camera. My only complaint is that the bulb is very, very white and draws most of the attention. Once again, love the shot. Keep shooting. --Mike', '2006-08-29 12:10:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2770646, 379000, 62009, '<td valign="top"><b>Greets from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>This is a very well done shot.  I would say that I would have cropped it just a little differently to get the whole camera in the scene on the right hand side.<br/> <br/>Also, there is quite a bit of glare on the lens on the right hand side.<br/> <br/>The sheet used for a backdrop is too wrinkled and doesn''t cover the entire BG.  Also, it shows where the harsher lighting is coming from, so there is an unevenness about the lighting.<br/> <br/>Otherwise,  I like the shot and think it was quite well done.<br/> <br/>--Mike</td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club  This is a very well done shot.  I would say that I would have cropped it just a little differently to get the whole camera in the scene on the right hand side. Also, there is quite a bit of glare on the lens on the right hand side. The sheet used for a backdrop is too wrinkled and doesn''t cover the entire BG.  Also, it shows where the harsher lighting is coming from, so there is an unevenness about the lighting. Otherwise,  I like the shot and think it was quite well done. --Mike', '2006-08-29 14:37:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2771297, 381106, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>Kudos on meeting the challenge criteria in a very imaginative way.  You have amazed me with how you have the reflection of a reflection in the camera lens so perfectly aligned with the original reflection that is captured by the camera.  It made me look twice cause the camera almost looks a bit transparent.  Why didn''t this score higher?  I think it is because of a couple of reasons.  First, the door to your right and the wall to your left cut the frame up in an unnecesary manner.  Second, the clutter to your left is unsightly.  Third, you have a subtle yellow tint from the tungsten lighting in the room.  Reshoot this with a sheet (or something similar) behind you and correct the white balance and this would be much more powerful of an image.<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: Kudos on meeting the challenge criteria in a very imaginative way.  You have amazed me with how you have the reflection of a reflection in the camera lens so perfectly aligned with the original reflection that is captured by the camera.  It made me look twice cause the camera almost looks a bit transparent.  Why didn''t this score higher?  I think it is because of a couple of reasons.  First, the door to your right and the wall to your left cut the frame up in an unnecesary manner.  Second, the clutter to your left is unsightly.  Third, you have a subtle yellow tint from the tungsten lighting in the room.  Reshoot this with a sheet (or something similar) behind you and correct the white balance and this would be much more powerful of an image. YoursTC', '2006-08-29 19:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2771470, 378502, 62009, '<td valign="top"><b>Greets from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Congrats on a great shot.  I really like this one.  I think it was one of the most innovative in the challenge.  <br/> <br/>I don''t think there''s much that I can say that hasn''t already been said.  <br/> <br/>I agree that something other than the carpet should have been used, but the soft texture of it does add to the  hardness of the doorknob.<br/> <br/>Also, having something behind the camera would have helped immensely.  The other commenters mentioned a black or white background.  I''d suggest a medium blue to contrast the silver. And also, as you mentioned, the scars on the doorknob aren''t the best idea, but I don''t think they distract too much.<br/> <br/>If you''d like, PM me about this critique.  Also, please be sure to mark that it was helpful, if, in fact, it is.<br/> <br/>--Mike</td>', 'Greets from the Critique Club  Congrats on a great shot.  I really like this one.  I think it was one of the most innovative in the challenge.   I don''t think there''s much that I can say that hasn''t already been said.   I agree that something other than the carpet should have been used, but the soft texture of it does add to the  hardness of the doorknob. Also, having something behind the camera would have helped immensely.  The other commenters mentioned a black or white background.  I''d suggest a medium blue to contrast the silver. And also, as you mentioned, the scars on the doorknob aren''t the best idea, but I don''t think they distract too much. If you''d like, PM me about this critique.  Also, please be sure to mark that it was helpful, if, in fact, it is. --Mike', '2006-08-29 21:08:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2771570, 380280, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>First off, I LOVE reading your description!  Isn''t amazing the things we do to get pictures sometimes.  I will go look at the setup in your portfolio in a bit.<br/> <br/>I thought this was a very good shot when I voted during the challenge - it wasn''t a static, head-on shot, which to me indicates a good imagination - you gave it some thought and effort and to me, it paid off.  I really like the color and lines created by the intersections of the mirrors.  The slightly different angles give each reflection a slightly different look, which creates interest and keeps the viewer engaged.<br/> <br/>The lighting is good - I like that there''s no significant glare in the lens face.  Focus is pretty good, particularly for a reflection.  The word "Nikon" could be just a tad sharper but again, since it''s a reflection, that''s hard to do.<br/> <br/>A well done shot, and a great interpretation of the challenge.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club First off, I LOVE reading your description!  Isn''t amazing the things we do to get pictures sometimes.  I will go look at the setup in your portfolio in a bit. I thought this was a very good shot when I voted during the challenge - it wasn''t a static, head-on shot, which to me indicates a good imagination - you gave it some thought and effort and to me, it paid off.  I really like the color and lines created by the intersections of the mirrors.  The slightly different angles give each reflection a slightly different look, which creates interest and keeps the viewer engaged. The lighting is good - I like that there''s no significant glare in the lens face.  Focus is pretty good, particularly for a reflection.  The word "Nikon" could be just a tad sharper but again, since it''s a reflection, that''s hard to do. A well done shot, and a great interpretation of the challenge.', '2006-08-29 22:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2771709, 381204, 30982, '<td valign="top">You have a winter room?  Near the potty?  Do I really want to know?  I gave you a 6 - I liked the lighting.  Better shot that mine, that''s for sure.  And mine was all your fault, you know...<br/> <br/>Know any songs after the 80s?  :-)</td>', 'You have a winter room?  Near the potty?  Do I really want to know?  I gave you a 6 - I liked the lighting.  Better shot that mine, that''s for sure.  And mine was all your fault, you know... Know any songs after the 80s?  :-)', '2006-08-29 23:08:42.000000', NULL, 0),
